{"id":"313d56c5-9108-470f-81c1-04166a121b91","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"8b694b962c48b3a3","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/integration.ts","baseline":{"blob":"451afb664a44f7e39c717d8c8f861910a6bcd7b4","start":1681,"end":1805},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","const","commandFinished","=","(","exitCode","?",":","number",")",":","string","=>","`","","${","OSC","}","D","${","exitCode","===","undefined","?","\"","","\"",":","\"",";","\"","+","exitCode","}","","${","BEL","}","","`"]},"context":{"before":"f2954f56a2c5a5bd","after":"d1e0c498f528c026"}},"payload":{"text":"It finished, with its exit code (D) — or, with none, the command line was abandoned before it ran.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:07:56.242Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:07:56.242Z"}
{"id":"54e1f24b-e8ec-4125-b664-2a0a3778646d","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"f7f55a14688637ec","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/integration.ts","baseline":{"blob":"ec7f0ed29f5cc940262042d361db75c75241018f","start":919,"end":1102},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["function","escape","(","value",":","string",")",":","string","{","return","value",".","replaceAll","(","/","[\\\\;\\x00-\\x20]","/","gu",",","(","char",")","=>","(","char","===","\"","\\","\\\\","\\","\"","?","\"","\\","\\\\\\\\","\\","\\","\\","\"",":","`","\\","\\\\x","\\","${","char",".","charCodeAt","(","0",")",".","toString","(","16",")",".","padStart","(","2",",","\"","0","\"",")","}","","`",")",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"3e05a66fda981434","after":"5e50779659d5133a"}},"payload":{"text":"A value as VS Code reads it in a sequence: backslash, `;` and control characters (and space) escaped as `\\xNN`.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:07:57.206Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:07:57.206Z"}
{"id":"ae2a7fe1-f19c-4ca3-af74-077420a7ba47","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"fda0a5bd83898e91","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/integration.ts","baseline":{"blob":"3e08bef0cbf5da038223f445ee91f1ca3767503a","start":1,"end":24},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","OSC","=","\"","\\","\\x1B]633;","x","1B","\""]},"context":{"after":"3e05a66fda981434"}},"payload":{"text":"VS Code shell integration for our terminal: the OSC 633 sequences a desktop shell's integration script prints (bash,\nzsh, pwsh), so VS Code knows where each prompt and command starts, what was run, where, and how it ended — just as\nit would for a real shell. With them, the terminal gets VS Code's own command decorations (a dot by each command,\nred when it failed), command navigation and sticky scroll, and extensions get the public shell-integration API\n(`terminal.shellIntegration`, `window.onDidStart/EndTerminalShellExecution` with the command line and exit code) —\nthe extension point a desktop extension would use to see what runs in a terminal.\n\nA shell VS Code starts itself is handed a nonce to sign its command lines with; ours isn't, so they arrive marked\nuntrusted (`commandLine.isTrusted` false), still at high confidence.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:07:57.486Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:07:57.486Z"}
{"id":"d648ce8c-2f04-4baf-81e4-7106f686814a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"5e50779659d5133a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/integration.ts","baseline":{"blob":"254c4b442ed98940781889cf280e5f9d6ef9781f","start":1223,"end":1279},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","const","promptStart","=","(",")",":","string","=>","`","","${","OSC","}","A","${","BEL","}","","`"]},"context":{"before":"f7f55a14688637ec","after":"25962d05591b200b"}},"payload":{"text":"A prompt starts (A) — before it's drawn.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:07:56.525Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:07:56.525Z"}
